{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nplan={\\\"description\\\":\\\"Discriminator: two commands are marshalled back to back (a 70000-byte value followed by a small one); after the first is unmarshalled, does the second decode to what was written? Prefix: the harness builds both commands and marshals them into one buffer with the implementation's own codec. Controls: the prerequisite prints the written keys and lengths and the total wire bytes, and the result prints the decoded first-value length, the second command's decoded fields, whether they match and how many bytes remain.\\\",\n \\\"claim_id\\\":\\\"C10-command-value-length-survives-the-wire\\\",\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB11-value-codec\\\"],\n \\\"harness\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"go_test\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"In-package Go test that writes two commands into one stream and decodes them in order, reporting what the second one becomes.\\\",\n  \\\"semantic_changes\\\":[\\\"harness-only scaffolding: no replica is constructed; the test calls the state codec directly on a buffer holding two commands\\\",\\\"two commands in one buffer model a batch or a recorder that appends commands, which is how the implementation writes them\\\"],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"stream_built\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"stream_marshalled\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"second_key\\\",\\\"value\\\":2},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"first_bytes\\\",\\\"value\\\":70000}]}],\n  \\\"legality\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB11-value-codec\\\"],\n   \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The wire form of a command sequence is exactly concatenated Command marshallings, which is what batches and the durable record append.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"One stream, two commands, no replica.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"the durable recorder's own append order is a separate observation\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}},\n \\\"monitors\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M1-stream-shift\\\",\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH2-stream-shift\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"stream_shifted\\\",\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB11-value-codec\\\"],\n   \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB11-value-codec\\\"],\n    \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The event reports what the second command decoded to and how many bytes remain, which is the consequence of the truncated length.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"The first command carried a value beyond the length field's range.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"stream\\\",\\\"reference\\\":\\\"stream_built.stream\\\"}],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"stream_built\\\"}],\n \\\"observable_properties\\\":[{\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH2-stream-shift\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"event_assertion\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"stream_shifted\\\"},\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"second_matches\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"stream\\\"],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"The command following an oversized value must still decode to what was written.\\\"}],\n \\\"uncertainties\\\":[\\\"the check does not attach the shifted stream to a replica reader, so the reader's own reaction is unobserved\\\",\\\"the shipped configuration's 1000-byte commands never reach the boundary\\\"]}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"check\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"unit-C10-command-value-length-survives-the-wire\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Second scenario for the same obligation, covering the consequence the first check left open: the leftover bytes of a truncated value shift the stream, so the next command in the same buffer decodes to garbage. The harness writes a 70000-byte value followed by a small command and decodes both in order; the local construction run shows the second command with op 197, an arbitrary key and a 53198-byte value, with 12341 bytes remaining, so the trust the codec places in the length field destroys the following command as well. The trusted runner and a fresh correspondence review decide the formal outcome.\\\",\n \\\"plan_path\\\":\\\"plan-stream-shift.json\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"explore_value_len2_test.go\\\",\\\"files\\\":{}}\njson.dump(plan,open('plan-stream-shift.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-stream-shift.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-stream-shift.json 2>&1 | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
